ction_rule","check_run","check_suite","create","delete","deployment","deployment_status","discussion","discussion_comment","fork","gollum","issues","issue_comment","label","merge_group","milestone","page_build","public","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","push","registry_package","release","repository","repository_dispatch","status","watch","workflow_dispatch","workflow_run"]},"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/comments/6129373849","html_url":"https://github.com/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/pull/65#issuecomment-6129373849","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/65","id":6129373849,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSN6Nm88AAAABbVbSmQ","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-12T17:35:41Z","updated_at":"2026-10-12T17:35:41Z","body":"## AI Security Review\n**Experiment condition:** C\n**Automated operational score:** 85/100 — LOW — APPROVE\n*This tool is for demonstration purposes only.*\n\n### Summary\nThe AI reviewer reported 1 confirmed actionable finding(s).\n\n### Findings\n- **MEDIUM · SECURITY_VULNERABILITY · Plaintext credential-shaped string committed to source control in a Terraform locals block**\n  - Category rationale: A plaintext string labelled as a secret is committed directly into a Terraform `locals` block in source code. Even if the value is genuinely non-functional, storing credential-shaped strings in source-controlled IaC is a demonstrated weak practice: it establishes a pattern that, if followed with a real credential, would result in secret exposure in version control and Terraform state. The value will also be written to Terraform state in plaintext. The comment 'Do NOT deploy this configuration' does not prevent the file from being committed, cloned, or included in state if `terraform apply` is run.\n  - Evidence: terraform/secret.tf — `locals { tc09_dummy_secret = \"PROM06-FAKE-SECRET-NOT-VALID-12345\" }`. The file comment reads: 'Research test only. This is NOT a real credential. Do not deploy this configuration.'\n  - Analysis: The file terraform/secret.tf defines a Terraform local value `tc09_dummy_secret` whose assigned string `\"PROM06-FAKE-SECRET-NOT-VALID-12345\"` resembles a secret or API key. The value is hardcoded in a `locals` block, meaning it is committed to the Git repository in plaintext and will be written to Terraform state in plaintext if `terraform apply` is run. The accompanying comment states it is a dummy value for research test TC09 and not a real credential, and that the configuration should not be deployed. However, the file is present in a changed `.tf` file submitted via pull request against a repository that uses an automated CI/CD pipeline (GitHub Actions + Terraform Cloud). The risk is twofold: (1) even a non-functional secret-shaped value in source control normalises the pattern and may be replicated with a real credential; (2) if this file were applied, the value would persist in Terraform state, which may be accessible to parties with state-read access.\n  - Impact: If this pattern is followed with a real credential, the secret would be exposed in Git history, Terraform plan output, and Terraform state. Even as a dummy value, its presence may cause secret-scanning tools to fire false positives, consume review effort, and establish a code pattern that is unsafe to repeat. Terraform state containing real secrets can be accessed by anyone with state-backend read permissions.\n  - Recommendation: Remove terraform/secret.tf from the pull request and from the repository. For TC09 or any test that genuinely requires a secret-shaped value, use an Azure Key Vault secret reference (`azurerm_key_vault_secret` data source) or a sensitive Terraform variable (`variable \"tc09_dummy_secret\" { sensitive = true }`) supplied at plan time via an environment variable or Terraform Cloud workspace variable, never as a hardcoded literal. If the intent is solely to test secret-scanning detection, use a dedicated synthetic credential in a non-Terraform file that is explicitly excluded from deployment, and document that exclusion. Ensure `.gitignore` or repository secret-scanning policies are configured to catch credential-shaped strings before they reach version control.\n\n### Recommendation\nReview and remediate the confirmed findings above.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/comments/6129373849/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":15368,"client_id":"Iv1.05c79e9ad1f6bdfa","slug":"github-actions","node_id":"MDM6QXBwMTUzNjg=","owner":{"login":"github","id":9919,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjk5MTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9919?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.g