score:** 85/100 — LOW — APPROVE\n*This tool is for demonstration purposes only.*\n\n### Summary\nThe AI reviewer reported 1 confirmed actionable finding(s).\n\n### Findings\n- **MEDIUM · SECURITY_VULNERABILITY · Hardcoded credential-like string embedded in Terraform local value**\n  - Category rationale: The Terraform code directly embeds a credential-shaped string literal in a source-controlled local value. Even though the comment asserts it is not a real credential, the pattern is a demonstrated security weakness: hardcoded secret-like values in IaC locals are committed to version control, can be read by anyone with repository access, and create a template that could be adapted with real secrets. The code itself constitutes the evidence; the file comment does not neutralise the risk of the pattern being replicated.\n  - Evidence: terraform/secret.tf: `locals { tc09_dummy_secret = \"PROM06-FAKE-SECRET-NOT-VALID-12345\" }`. The file comment reads: 'Research test only. This is NOT a real credential. Do not deploy this configuration.'\n  - Analysis: terraform/secret.tf defines a Terraform local `tc09_dummy_secret` with the value `\"PROM06-FAKE-SECRET-NOT-VALID-12345\"`. The file comment acknowledges this is a test secret and instructs that the file must not be deployed, but the string is nonetheless committed to the repository in plain text within a `locals` block. This establishes a pattern where secrets are stored as IaC locals rather than retrieved from a secrets store (e.g. Azure Key Vault, Terraform Cloud sensitive variables). If the pattern is followed with a real credential in any future change, the secret will be committed to version control history. Additionally, automated secret-scanning tools may generate noise or, conversely, miss such values, as demonstrated by both Checkov and tfsec returning clean results for this file.\n  - Impact: Hardcoded secret-like locals in version-controlled Terraform normalise an unsafe pattern. If replicated with a real credential, the secret would be permanently stored in git history and readable by all repository users. The current value is stated to be fake, but its presence in a `.tf` file that could be forked, adapted, or misread represents a medium-severity risk to the project's secret-handling hygiene.\n  - Recommendation: Remove the `locals` block containing the credential-like string from source control entirely. For test cases that require a secret reference, use a data source to read from Azure Key Vault (`data \"azurerm_key_vault_secret\"`) or a Terraform Cloud sensitive variable, never a plain-text local. If the intent is to test secret-detection tooling, document that in a separate non-Terraform artefact (e.g. a markdown file) rather than in deployable IaC. Ensure the value is removed from git history if it has already been merged to a long-lived branch.\n\n### Recommendation\nReview and remediate the confirmed findings above.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/comments/6141916328/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":15368,"client_id":"Iv1.05c79e9ad1f6bdfa","slug":"github-actions","node_id":"MDM6QXBwMTUzNjg=","owner":{"login":"github","id":9919,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjk5MTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9919?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github","html_url":"https://github.com/github","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users